klatt: flat wideband noise, user tuning carried onto upstream wideband base

Upstream restructured the wide path into klatt_wide.c (off unless
EVV_WIDE asks), so the old wide_on arm is gone with the old file.
What remains of the tuning is its noise half: shaping stays off
and NOISE_BAND stays at 7500 Hz so frication passes unshaped at
wideband rates. Rewritten against c3a253f; the old 0003 cannot
apply there.
diff --git a/src/klatt/klatt_fx.c b/src/klatt/klatt_fx.c
index bec56b1..54899bd 100644
--- a/src/klatt/klatt_fx.c
+++ b/src/klatt/klatt_fx.c
@@ -343,11 +343,11 @@ uint64_t fx_isqrt(uint64_t v)
  * EVV_NOISE=flat asks for the old behaviour at any rate, which is what the
  * two are measured against. */
 
-#define NOISE_BAND 5512
+#define NOISE_BAND 7500
 
 static int noise_shaping(void)
 {
